loading: let prefill admit into the RAM cache when the cache can hold most of the model -- prefill used cache=False to protect the decode working set, which on a 371GB box means every one of its ~9600 expert reads is discarded and then re-read by decode. Measured on L20: a single 126.5s prefill did 14896 disk reads (~280GB) while the cache held only 902 distinct experts, a 16.5x repeated read, and that read path is what pinned the CPU at 189 percent with the GPU at 0-16